<title>BRAZIL: Brazil May petroleum use up from April - Petrobras.</title>
<headline>Brazil May petroleum use up from April - Petrobras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumption in Brazil of petroleum products averaged 1,646,200 barrels per day (bpd) in May, up 1.3 percent from April, state-controlled oil company Petrobras said in a statement.</p>
<p>The figure represents a 7.4 percent increase on the same month last year, it added.</p>
<p>Of the total, diesel accounted for 533,700 barrels bpd and gasoline 286,300 bpd, Petrobras said.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
